Dance Pictogram — Cue Library
Data licence, version 1.0

WHAT THIS COVERS

The files in this repository: index.json, the ZIP packs, and everything inside them
(manifest.json, beats.json, fp.npz, pictograms/, real/). Referred to below as "the Data".

The Dance Pictogram application is licensed separately and is not covered here.


GRANT

You may download, store, and use the Data for personal, non-commercial purposes — practising
and learning dance routines, on your own devices, with the Dance Pictogram application or
your own tools.

No fee is charged for this.


CONDITIONS

You may not:

  1. sell, license, or otherwise commercialise the Data, in whole or in part, or include it
     in a paid or ad-supported product or service;

  2. redistribute the Data or bulk mirrors of it. Link to this repository instead. (This is
     not about control: a mirror cannot receive the takedowns and corrections described
     below, so it degrades into a copy nobody can fix.)

  3. use the Data to train, fine-tune, or evaluate machine-learning models;

  4. present the Data, or anything derived from it, as your own work, or strip the attribution
     and provenance information in index.json and the manifests.


THIRD-PARTY RIGHTS

The Data is derived from dance videos published on PyPyDance. The choreography, the
performances, the music, and the video recordings remain the property of their respective
rights holders. Nothing here grants you any right in them.

The `real/` images are derived directly from frames of those videos. The `pictograms/` images
are original artwork produced by this project's renderer.

No audio and no video is distributed here, and neither can be reconstructed from these files.
The `fp.npz` fingerprints are one-way spectral landmark hashes, not recordings.

If you hold rights in any routine represented here and want it removed, open a discussion on
this repository or contact the maintainer. Removal requests are honoured.


NO WARRANTY

The Data is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The cues are generated
automatically and are frequently imperfect. Dancing is physical activity: use your own
judgement, and do not rely on these cues for anything where being wrong would matter.

To the extent permitted by law, the maintainer is not liable for any claim, damage, or other
liability arising from the Data or its use.


CHANGES

Later versions of this licence may be published for later releases. The version distributed
alongside a given release governs that release.
